      "dimension_name": "Confidence calibration",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "Claude’s judgment that pe_004’s “confident” is defensible is correct and well reasoned: the same county, the same Thomas Flynn household, and an exact ten-year age progression from the 1850 census. The LLM deducts for the stored rationale being thin, but that’s a rationale-quality issue in a fixture-written entry, not a calibration error by Claude. Claude flagged it as such and asked before changing anything. Its recommendation to link a_008 and a_009 at the same tier is also sound, since they belong to the same persona."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_person_evidence_024",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "Lane discipline held: Claude made no add_relationship call and wrote no ParentChild edge. It minted Bridget through the correct persona form (recordRole: \"mother\"), with no duplicate and no extra facts. The LLM’s main complaint, holding the child-side links, is explicitly correct per the judge context. One small miss: the reply never says outright that the edge is deferred to proof-conclusion. But not writing it is what this test grades."
    },
