      "dimension_name": "Rationale quality",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The judge context says the stored rationale is fixture-written and “never scored against the agent,” yet the LLM docks the score for it. What counts is whether the review spotted the gaps, and it did: no cross-source corroboration, no ruling out of competing candidates, the a_012 birthplace left unaddressed, and an unexplained null score. The proposed fix covers all of them. One small slip: Claude calls c_001 a “core identifier conflict” without noting it’s already resolved. But it correctly says the conflict doesn’t undermine identity and doesn’t downgrade the link."
    },
